      "writtenOn": "2020-11-24T16:45:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can\u0027t use the config option here because the desired default value changes per port. This piece of code was added more as a quick modification to set DRP outside of having a chipset hook. Later in the stack, I have CL that fixes some issues in usbc related to setting the default power role.\n\nNote, that our TCPMv2 very much assumes a typical chromebook port. I have a CL that fixes this along with force_source (which currently is broken in TOT TCPMv2). I added a #ifdef guard for chipset_task around the code that assumes there is a chipset task that will control the DRP state and the #else path includes an overridable function to return desired starting port role so there is no timing uncertainty.\n\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/2541882",
